Package: HDGR
Title: Group Regression With Tailored Penalties for High-Dimensional Data With or Without Predefined Groups
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Reza", "Drikvandi", email = "reza.drikvandi@durham.ac.uk",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9958-0422"))
Description: Implements the main method (Case 3) of Drikvandi (2026)
    <doi:10.1111/sjos.70072> for high-dimensional group regression with
    a ridge penalty for the group of interest and a lasso penalty for the
    pooled nuisance predictors. Users can supply group labels and identify
    the group of interest, or use group correlation learning to form groups
    when labels are unavailable. Note that supplying only the group of interest places
    all remaining predictors in one nuisance group as in the paper. Provides coefficient
    estimates, debiased estimates for the group of interest, confidence
    intervals, and two-sided hypothesis tests.
